19:31:56 [05da] 
19:31:56 [05da] <the full story text>
19:31:56 [05da] 
19:31:56 [05da] ** End **
19:31:56 [05da] ** Takeaways **
19:31:56 [05da] - <takeaway 1: one short, kid-friendly sentence stating a lesson the child should learn>
19:31:56 [05da] - <takeaway 2: another lesson the story demonstrates>
19:31:56 [05da] - <takeaway 3: another lesson (optional)>
19:31:56 [05da] 
19:31:56 [05da] ** Explanation of the output **
19:31:56 [05da] <1–3 short sentences explaining how the story matches the selected topic(s) and the learning goals: general speech-language therapy goals>
19:31:56 [05da] 
19:31:56 [05da] STRICT RULES:
19:31:56 [05da] - HARD WORD LIMIT: The story text between ** Title ** and ** End ** MUST be 130–200 words. 200 is a CEILING you cannot exceed. Target around 165 words so you have safety margin. Count as you write; if you approach 200, wrap up immediately at the next natural sentence — do not start a new subplot, paragraph, or piece of dialogue.
19:31:56 [05da] - Brevity beats completeness. Cut adjectives, side details, and extra dialogue exchanges before going over.
19:31:56 [05da] - Do NOT include any preamble, commentary, or meta-text (no "Here is your story", "Sure!", etc.).
19:31:56 [05da] - Do NOT add sections beyond Title, story text, End, Takeaways, and Explanation.
19:31:56 [05da] Do not add any other sections or extra text.
19:31:56 [05da] 
